{"title":"2021 JMPSC Invitationals Problems/Problem 10","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Invitationals_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is chosen in isosceles trapezoid <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b44beb78e8be18179bfb7fe6b3424e7fb1aef32.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/8/4483542fa46123b1e899eda06f3de671df25bd07.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC=20$\" width=\"70\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/4/254e7e0278f8ac462ed26c600a8bbd800b86e1bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD=28$\" width=\"71\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/3/ab3e775e3fa4f944039a9d682ecb0f7542f7bc33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DA=20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" />. If the sum of the areas of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/8/e0830febe7535fbbdf19782a978c79c0c9e6cd70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PBC$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/9/249e729f8542ff5cfba842850a5efd1bc66e217e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PDA$\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/f/50ff9540650f0f95f80da2f6692fc8ee413e2eb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$144$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" />, then the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/5/4f550db59d15933de1a0871aaa917acdd99966af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PAB$\" width=\"41\" height=\"13\" /> can be written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/8/888fed89e19182447f85b3cb6676548a49395284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m}{n},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"27\" height=\"34\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/b/5db26f75f6218a382840f0ed34f5d36bcff61d33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"56\" height=\"14\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Invitationals_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We have the area of the trapezoid is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/7/a277f19c385f17e3d29b56abad9665ce15c81172.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16 \\cdot 16=256$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"103\" height=\"14\" /> since the height is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Now, subtracting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/f/50ff9540650f0f95f80da2f6692fc8ee413e2eb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$144$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" /> we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/6/726280df8d87469b4386b4e5cf0526584fc8d08c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$224=4x+28(16-x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"178\" height=\"20\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is the height of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/3/1636251674ae38bb58e9b70b6d64717afdcf942a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle PAB$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" />. This means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/5/c557944e0601d2c896d253f03084ca6d3670ebca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\frac{28}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"59\" height=\"38\" />, asserting the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/3/1636251674ae38bb58e9b70b6d64717afdcf942a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle PAB$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/8/5388ef88079e91c0f4942f22553aa367127e531a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{56}{3} \\implies 56+3=\\boxed{59}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"182\" height=\"38\" /> \n</p><p>~Geometry285, edited by CyclicISLscelesTrapezoid\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Invitationals_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ol><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Invitationals_Problems\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Invitationals Problems\">Other 2021 JMPSC Invitationals Problems</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Invitationals_Answer_Key\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Invitationals Answer Key\">2021 JMPSC Invitationals Answer Key</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=JMPSC_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"JMPSC Problems and Solutions\">All JMPSC Problems and Solutions</a></li></ol>\n<p>The problems on this page are copyrighted by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://jmpsc.org\">Junior Mathematicians' Problem Solving Competition</a>. <span class=\"mw-valign-middle\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:JMPSC.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/a/ab/JMPSC.png/120px-JMPSC.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"120\" height=\"120\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/a/ab/JMPSC.png/180px-JMPSC.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/a/ab/JMPSC.png 2x\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018015917\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.022 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.038 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 126/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 183/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3885/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.209      1 Template:JMPSC_Notice\n100.00%    5.209      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:21638:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018015917 and revision id 227906. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}